From 1574cded6f3180d4a95522f529f70bbdc9029afe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:15:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] kosmickrisp: read custom resolve input attachments from
 the attachments

VK_EXT_custom_resolve says reads from a resolving fragment shader's input
attachments read the multisampled colour or depth attachment. KosmicKrisp
lowered them to descriptor reads, so the result depended on whatever
image the application had bound. Native Half-Life: Alyx binds a
single-sample placeholder there, so its resolved scene was black.

For pipelines created with customResolve, rewrite input attachment
texel fetches to take their texture from a new root table array, picked
through the input attachment index map. vkCmdBeginCustomResolveEXT fills
that array with the multisampled colour, depth and stencil attachments.
The custom resolve flag and colour input map join the fragment shader
key. Also adds the KK_CUSTOM_RESOLVE_DEBUG=log view and descriptor
logging used to find this.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

